## Remediation User Token — Current State and Planned Approach

The remediation pod user and token were created manually during early setup, not via Terraform. At the
time, the Proxmox users TF module didn't exist and it was needed quickly for a running pod. Token stored
directly in Vault, pod fetches it at runtime.

The TF-managed approach is drafted but implementation is scoped to a later session (June at earliest).
The pattern when it gets implemented:

```hcl
resource "proxmox_virtual_environment_user" "remediation_user" {
  user_id = "remediation@pve"
  enabled = true
}

resource "proxmox_virtual_environment_user_token" "user_token" {
  token_name = "tk1"
  user_id    = proxmox_virtual_environment_user.remediation_user.user_id
}
```

The token value will be in Terraform state (marked sensitive by the provider, not printed in logs). The
flow would be: TF creates token → value stored in encrypted S3 state → pushed to Vault → pod fetches
from Vault at runtime. Token never appears in logs or config files.

The same approach will be used to import the existing `k8s-pve` user that was created manually during
the remediation pod preparation phase. Both are deferred, both have a clear path.

