## Known Uncovered Security Risks

**1. Permanent Proxmox API token with full admin scope**

The token never expires and has Administrator privileges inherited from root ACL. If compromised, manual
revocation is required (`pveum user token remove`). No auto-expiry, no rotation mechanism currently.
Accepted — the token only exists in Secrets Manager with restricted access, and PVE realm isolation
prevents OS-level pivot. Rotation and scoped tokens per operation are the future direction when the users
module is implemented.

**2. Manually created users not under Terraform control**

The remediation user, its token, and the k8s-pve user were created manually and are outside the
infrastructure-as-code state. If something changes on those (permissions, expiry, deletion) there is no
TF drift detection. Accepted as a known gap with a documented plan to bring them under Terraform control
in a later session.